Haybarn CI

This repository is a fork of duckdb/duckdb-ci (https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-ci),
maintained by Query Farm LLC for Haybarn, an independent derived distribution of
DuckDB. Haybarn is not affiliated with or endorsed by the DuckDB Foundation.
DuckDB is a trademark of the DuckDB Foundation.

Upstream duckdb/duckdb-ci ships no LICENSE file. Like the DuckDB Foundation's
other repositories it is treated here as MIT-licensed; the accompanying LICENSE
reproduces the DuckDB MIT license and its copyright notice.

Haybarn modifications are kept as a small commit stack on top of upstream
`main` (branch `haybarn`). They:

- make the container registry of the extension build/test matrix configurable
  (`matrix` action input `image_registry`), defaulting to Haybarn's registry so
  Haybarn builds never run in DuckDB's images;
- add a workflow that publishes the build images under that registry;
- clone gcompat (alpine aarch64 cpp/test images) from the Query-farm-haybarn/gcompat
  mirror, because git.adelielinux.org is unreachable from GitHub-hosted runners.
  Keep the mirror in step when upstream moves GCOMPAT_REF.

Upstream's own workflows (ci.yml, pages.yml, prune-dev-images.yml) target
DuckDB's infrastructure and are disabled in this repository's Actions settings
rather than edited, so rebases stay clean. A workflow file that a rebase adds
starts out enabled: after each rebase, review `gh workflow list` and disable
any new upstream workflow.
